+# Fork provenance
+
+This directory is a fork of NoMount's kernel sources.
+
+upstream  = https://github.com/maxsteeel/nomount
+commit    = 016375cd4a9e7da07b0519dd7bc492101de2a834
+date      = 2026-09-13
+protocol  = "20"
+imported  = Hybrid Mount commit 4485e41c (verbatim import, original filenames nomount.c / nomount.h)
+license   = GPL-2.0-only, see LICENSE in this directory. Upstream shipped a GPL-3.0 text
+            while the kernel module declared a bare MODULE_LICENSE("GPL"); this module is
+            distributed under the GPL-2.0-only grant and declares MODULE_LICENSE("GPL v2")
+            so the declaration, the SPDX headers and the license text agree.
+            See ../../THIRD_PARTY.md.
+
+## Imported baseline (sha256, exactly as imported)
+
+f2bc043af419e857e920fb193e42f3b98b32b432ff58ecc4fd722526f97c5c77  nomount.c
+21e34e1c16a2870d464a0f1cf669f976695d2435cbd661c7b3e40f4f8303b6cd  nomount.h
+c85c0ebe247c77882c5ac9f776941bf3a50f859b7d6bfb5bca1e1ccf9bed5b47  Makefile
+1df7ad3589a282128f797f7a46b28aee315d080550aae26b681a898f11c7abc7  Kconfig
+3972dc9744f6499f0f9b2dbf76696f2ae7ad8af9b23dde66d6af86c9dfb36986  LICENSE
+c42cad879c216d643444b448e8bd461a757cc2754e716520c9d36da6e799324f  UPSTREAM_README.md
+
+These digests describe the files exactly as imported, under their original names. The
+working tree has since diverged; in particular LICENSE no longer matches the imported
+GPL-3.0 text. To compare against the pristine baseline, use the import commit:
+
+    git show 4485e41c:module/vfs/src/nomount.c
+
+## Hybrid Mount divergence applied so far
+
+- License: GPL-2.0-only text in LICENSE, `SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only` in
+  every source file, and MODULE_LICENSE("GPL v2") in the module.
+- Identity: files, include guard, key type name, protocol version, Kconfig symbol,
+  Makefile object, module description, and the kernel log prefix, now "hybridmount:".
+- Internal symbols: nomount_* -> hybridmount_*, nm_* -> hm_*, NM_* -> HM_*.
+- Wire magic: HYBRIDMOUNT_MAGIC_SIG is now the HM-exclusive 0x4859425249444D4F
+  (ASCII "HYBRIDMO"), replacing upstream's 0x4E4F4D4F554E54 ("NOMOUNT"). It is also the
+  full_name_hash seed and must match src/vfs/protocol.rs::MAGIC byte for byte.
+- Virtual offset signature: HM_SIG_16 is 'hm' (0x686D), replacing 'nm' (0x6E6D). It is
+  the high half of the packed virtual loff_t, so it is an in-kernel ABI in its own right.
+- HM_FLAG_OPAQUE (bit 3) is a new flag: an opaque directory replaces its whole subtree,
+  stays visible and shows only the injected children. The userspace emits it for a
+  .replace directory and for every directory below it, matching Magisk semantics.
+- Batch ADD_RULE reports the first failure and the offset of the failing record;
+  DEL_RULE does the same and no longer leaves status 0 on a truncated batch. A rule
+  whose real path cannot be resolved is rejected with -ENOENT, an out-of-range cursor
+  with -EINVAL, and a failed directory-node allocation with -ENOMEM.
+- The isolated-uid table stays sorted, so the per-lookup isolation check bisects instead
+  of scanning every entry.
+- Builds for pre-5.18 kernels need -std=gnu11, which the Makefile sets.
+- Rules attached to a real directory retain its path for their registered lifetime.
+  This keeps the inode carrying the lookup/iterate hooks alive under cache reclaim;
+  generated virtual ancestors retain the same reference when they attach to a real
+  parent. Retired rules release it after the existing RCU/SRCU reader drain, including
+  replacement, rollback, deletion and clear before module teardown restores VFS ops.
+- Selective upstream review through NoMount dev
+  71ff9c4cd3037e3c968263a1d82b447f511cc658 (2026-10-04 review):
+  - 60073edc / fd1201a4: initialize virtual inodes before publishing them and reuse
+    existing inodes without allocating a spare. Unlike upstream's initializing
+    sentinel, fully initialized candidates compete via cmpxchg; the loser detaches
+    its directory association before eviction. Failed igrab is handled explicitly.
+    Eviction protects the node with RCU and retires an empty inode slot atomically
+    before freeing orphan topology, so an old inode cannot free a new owner's node.
+    Rule retirement publishes orphan ownership before checking the inode slot, so
+    concurrent eviction cannot leave an empty orphan node without a free claimant.
+  - 53e4c93e: clean up in evict_inode, retaining the original destroy_inode callback.
+    Virtual inodes restore their own mapping and use generic eviction; real inodes
+    restore their filesystem operations before calling the original evict_inode.
+  - 6a899d50: reuse existing virtual-parent topology without hooking it again or
+    retaining a parent-path reference to our own virtual inode.
+  - fea33dd0: skip the UID-table RCU section when no isolation table is installed.
+  The imported baseline above remains unchanged. ART, seqcount and SRCU are retained;
+  this is a selective port, not a wholesale upstream snapshot replacement.
+
+Behaviour is no longer byte-identical to upstream, and the wire magic no longer matches
+it: a stock nm CLI is rejected at preparse with -EFAULT. The payload field order, sizes
+and command numbering are still the upstream ones.
+
+## Syncing with upstream
+
+1. Fetch the upstream revision you want to compare against.
+2. Diff it against the commit recorded above and review every upstream change.
+3. Re-apply the Hybrid Mount divergences on top; never overwrite them blindly.
+4. Update this file (commit, date, digests) in the same commit as the sync.
